=== Villager gifts ===
{{see also|Tutorial:Raid farming}}
{{IN|Java}}, when the player has the [[Hero of the Village]] status effect, a mason [[villager]] might throw that player a clay block as a gift.

=== Post-generation ===
Placing [[mud]] above a block with a [[pointed dripstone]] hanging underneath the mud gives it a {{frac|45|256}} (about 17.6%) chance per [[random tick]] to convert into clay, with an average conversion time of 388.4 seconds. Mud does not convert in [[the Nether]].{{note|In {{in|je}}, this is controlled by the environment attribute <code>gameplay/water_evaporates</code>.}}<ref>{{bug|MC-264720|||WAI}}</ref> The dripstone does not deposit any water into a [[cauldron]], despite the dripping animation.

== Usage ==
[[Big dripleaves]], [[small dripleaves]], [[Mangrove Propagule|mangrove propagules]], [[azalea]]s, and [[flowering azalea]]s are the only plants that can be placed on clay. Unlike most other blocks, clay supports small dripleaves even outside of [[water]].

When an azalea or flowering azalea placed on a block of clay is grown into an [[azalea tree]], the clay block turns into [[rooted dirt]].

